# Selection lists

Single-choice pickers (language, device type, and similar) use **separate rounded rows** that match primary button shape — not one flat grouped table.

## Stacked picker rows

- Each row: `Radii.Button` (16), `1px` `Colors.Hairline`, `Colors.Card` fill, `Layout.MinControl` min height, `Space.md` horizontal padding.
- Stack with `Space.sm` gap inside screen margin `Space.screen`.
- Press state: `Colors.Hover` on the row. Selected state: seafoam `checkmark-circle` trailing icon (same as other pickers).
- Set `overflow: hidden` on the row so press fill clips to the radius.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — language / single-choice picker
<SList>
  {options.map((option) => (
    <SOption key={option.code} onPress={() => select(option.code)}>
      {({ pressed }) => (
        <SRow $pressed={pressed}>
          <SName>{option.nativeName}</SName>
          {selected ? <Ionicons name='checkmark-circle' color={Colors.Seafoam} /> : null}
        </SRow>
      )}
    </SOption>
  ))}
</SList>
```

## Grouped inset cards

When several rows share one white card (settings sections, wearable list), wrap them in `SCard` with `Radii.Card`, hairline border, and **`overflow: hidden`** so row backgrounds clip to the card corners.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — square corners when rows paint Card fill to the edges
const SCard = styled.View`
  border-radius: ${Radii.Card}px;
  background-color: ${Colors.Card};
`

// ✅ GOOD
const SCard = styled.View`
  border-radius: ${Radii.Card}px;
  background-color: ${Colors.Card};
  overflow: hidden;
`
```
